  "type": "Activity",
  "number": "1.4.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  What binary number comes after 11 ? Try it in the binary odometer above.          Correct! In binary, 11 represents the decimal number 3. Adding 1 triggers a carry that results in 100 (which represents 4).    12  Remember that binary numbers only use the digits 0 and 1.    Try it in the binary odometer above. It needs 3 bits.     "
