  "body": "  An overflow error occurs when there aren't enough bits to represent a given number. Which of following would cause an overflow error to occur. (Choose all that apply.)      Trying to represent 15 in 4 bits.    No, this would not cause an overflow. 15 is represented as 1111 in 4 bits.      Trying to represent 16 in 4 bits.    Yes. The largest number that can be represented in 4 bits is 15, which is 1111. To represent 16 you would need an additional bit, 1 0000.      Trying to represent 31 in 5 bits.    No, this would not cause an overflow. 31 is represented as 1 1111 in 5 bits.      Trying to represent 32 in 5 bits.    Yes. The largest number that can be represented in 5 bits is 31, which is 1 1111. To represent 32 you would need a 6th bit, 10 0000.     "
